visit the new york times website at  nytimes.com  and click on books  alexandra robbins tell me the story  behind secrets of the two  secrets of the tomb is an expose and an  analysis of probably the world's most  infamous secret society skull bones is  the society to which president george w  bush belongs it is also the society to  which senator john kerry belongs which  will make the presidential election of  2004 particularly interesting it'll be  the first bones versus bones ballot  are you a yellow yourself i am a yali i  graduated in 1998 i was a member of  another secret society however since  this book has been published i fear i  might not be a member anymore  what's the name of that one  the name of that secret society was  scroll and key which is also lumped with  skull and bones uh often however we  didn't have the death motif of skull and  bones we didn't have a tomb full of  skeletons and coffins and mummies and we  also don't follow the same agenda as  skull and bones which is basically to  get their members into positions of  power and then once those members are in  positions of power for them to hire  other members and and elevate their  stature which is something that bush has  done for members of skull and bones for  example who are some key people in the  administration who are skull and  bonesmen  one of george w bush's first  appointments was the assistant attorney  general of the justice department's  largest litigation component he's a  member of skull bones so is the general  counsel of the office of homeland  security bush's first choice for  secretary of defense was also a member  of skull bones frederick smith the ceo  of federal express but he had to  withdraw for health considerations  patronage is as old as the presidency so  why are you particularly interested or  concerned in this president of  appointing skull and bones people  i think a lot of people in america are  disturbed that a secret society can have  so much influence in the country it may  not be a coincidence that we have the  most secret government that we've seen  since the nixon era and that this secret  government full of  a super secret spy court and a shadow  government and leaders being whisked to  secret undisclosed locations i don't  think it's a coincidence that the  president is a member of the country's  most secret society if it's so secret  how are you able to tell the story  ah luck  i have been threatened by skull and  bones skull and bones  has made it known to me that it's angry  i was harassed they hung up on me but i  did manage to get more than 100 members  of skull and bones to speak with me and  i came across a sheath of documents that  revealed many of the secrets of the tomb  give me a for instance about some of the  revelations your readers will find in  the book sure  well i when i began this book i intended  to debunk many of the conspiracy  theories one surprise to me was that  many of the theories are based on  kernels of truth for example somebody  had had said to me that skull and bones  dropped the atom bomb i did not believe  it but i investigated it and it turns  out that henry stimpson the secretary of  war in world war ii uh was a member of  skull bones he hired other members of  skull and bones to work with him in the  war department he put those bonesmen in  charge of the deployment of the atomic  bomb so there are kernels of truth in  most every conspiracy theory about this  secret society  what should people know about your alma  mater that it fosters or allows these  kinds of organizations to exist a lot of  people ask me if these societies are so  terrible why does yale allow them to  insist while many members of the yale  administration are members of these  secret societies themselves is yale  alone in these kinds of societies  actually many schools especially ivy  league schools across america have  secret societies but skull and bones and  yale sacred societies have traditionally  stood very far apart and above the rest  i think it has something to do with the  the gothic elitism at yale tell me about  your writing career how did you become a  writer how did you get started in all  this  i started writing when i was 19 for a  very kind and generous editor at the  washington post  my first book was a book called quarter  life crisis which came out about a year  and a half ago  and then i decided to shift to something  a little more a little more serious and  to move my career in an investigative  journalism direction and that's what led  me to skull and bones are you writing  full-time books full-time and  are you making a living at it  i hope so i i write for magazines and  newspapers and i write books full time  now so we'll see how long i can keep it  going where's your home base washington  d.c  and what interests you next now that  you've done these two  i'm actually writing a third book now on  a secret organization however i'm  undercover this year so i'm not going to  tell you what the organization is  because that'll blow my case  well thank you for talking to us  alexander robin's book is called secrets  of the tomb skull and bones the ivy  league and the hidden paths of power  thank you  the men of the 23rd headquarters special  troops were recruited to become phantom  warriors in a ghost army for world war  ii
 

